{"agent":"bfix2-lane2","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_mirror_sibling_gates` only appends `review.triaged` events for the sibling gates; the settle pass is still run only for the gate that was explicitly triaged. For a combined `rubber_duck,critic` review where each gate has one triageable finding with the same digest and the gate cap is 1, triaging `rubber_duck` appends a `critic` `review.triaged` event, but after reload the code computes `counts` for `rubber_duck` and calls `_settle_after_cap(..., \"rubber_duck\", ...)`. No `_settle_after_cap` is run for `critic`, so `critic` can remain unsettled/open even though its only finding was just answered, leaving the agent to deal with the sibling gate again.","digest":"2efdc8d2c188201a","location":"ddflow/api/review/triaging.py:194","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/review/triaging.py:194"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The mirrored `review.triaged` events are appended for the sibling gates, but after `_load` the code still calls `_settle_after_cap` only for the original `gate`. A combined review with a single finding shows the defect: triaging `rubber_duck` #1 records a verdict for `critic` via `_mirror_sibling_gates`, yet only `rubber_duck` is passed to `_settle_after_cap`, so `critic` is never settled once its triage count reaches cap. The sibling gate remains unsettled, so the same finding can still be requested again for that gate, which is the original triaged-twice bug for any gate completed by mirroring rather than an explicit triage in that gate.","digest":"549d742ae4f7d570","location":"ddflow/api/review/triaging.py:213","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/review/triaging.py:213"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The new test directly uses external subprocess tools (`from conftest import run_cli`, `from helpers import git as _git`, and then `run_cli(...)` / `_git(...)`) rather than going through a port in `ddflow/adapters` and driving a fake. This violates [r-adapters] (advisory): git, filesystem layout, and subprocess tools are required to sit behind one adapter/port, and tests should use fakes instead of subprocesses. Since this is a new test file, the direct external dependencies make the change violate the project rule.","digest":"3bdf15723b2bbdff","location":"tests/test_review_triage_combined.py:15-16 and tests/test_review_triage_combined.py:_setup","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_review_triage_combined.py:15-16 and tests/test_review_triage_combined.py:_setup"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":7321,"diff_sha":"977ed5b513b128cc851557d5f28dd945f8173703ebf6dad5f7ebc1feae1ff166","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":553.8,"family":"alibaba","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"fd363c08da2ac4dd","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-combined-review-findings-triaged-twice.critic.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261103T085939Z-696dfd6a.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"dbd993da5e9c8014d61d37398fe277bb25284b49","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/review/findings.py":"100644 2441434636214b468d5272dce403d2e7b458bb57","ddflow/api/review/triaging.py":"100644 78c0e049763aa486c42dd7260042a875440b6659","tests/test_review_triage_combined.py":"100644 8e1f2740b4deb804e2902dc70ca46c9e4c6a7b48"},"reviewer":"qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/review/triaging.py:194","ddflow/api/review/triaging.py:213","tests/test_review_triage_combined.py:15-16 and tests/test_review_triage_combined.py:_setup"],"tree_sha":"dbd993da5e9c+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"3 finding(s)"},"id":"e25eb321f14a3ab4b59589f1e","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":131121,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-combined